– Certificates / forms:  
• Medical certificate provided for absence from work 22/11/25–28/11/25 for LRTI / probable atypical pneumonia.  
• Centrelink medical form: NOT completed today. To be done after review with results + response to tx (3–5 days). Documented that complex forms not done on brief phone-only consult without exam/obs. She unhappy but accepted short delay.

– Safety net:  
Advised ED/urgent review if SOB at rest / unable to speak full sentences, high fevers not settling, chest pain at rest, palpitations, confusion/syncope, haemoptysis. RTC if any deterioration.

– Follow-up:  
Booked F2F review 2–3 days (or earlier if worse) to:  
• check vitals, O2 sats, chest exam  
• review CXR + bloods  
• confirm dx and decide on duration off work  
• complete Centrelink form if ongoing functional impairment and pneumonia confirmed.

If can’t get in here, advised can see local GP/after-hours with same plan once results available on system.

She also briefly raised “months of exhaustion from double shifts / maybe burnout and mental health certificate”. Advised separate longer consult once acute illness settled – not addressed today due to time. She a bit frustrated about needing multiple visits.

